---
layout: layouts/base.vto
title: Marwan Ayman Shawky - Cloud & DevOps Engineer
description: Cloud & DevOps Engineer passionate about building scalable infrastructure and automating everything
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="term-card">
      <div class="term-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>marwan@cairo: ~</span></div>
      <div class="term-body">
        <div class="nameplate">
          <p class="prompt">$ whoami<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></p>
          <h1 class="name-lat">Marwan Ayman Shawky</h1>
          <p class="role">Cloud &amp; DevOps engineer. I keep other people's systems boring on purpose.</p>
          <div class="hero-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/maroayman">github</a>
            <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/maroayman">linkedin</a>
            <button class="copy-mail" id="copyMail" data-email="marwanayman.shawky@gmail.com" aria-label="Copy email address" title="Copy email address">email</button>
            <a href="/resume.pdf">resume.pdf</a>
            <a href="/blog">/blog →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="place">
            <span>Platform Engineer · Cairo, Egypt</span>
            <span>Open to remote</span>
          </div>
          <span class="avail"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Available for remote work</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about" id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ comp.page_header({ title: "About", level: "h2", cls: "", num: "01" }) }}
    <div class="about-cols">
      <div>
        <p class="lede">I build the unglamorous half of the stack: pipelines that fail loudly and roll back quietly, alerts that wake a human only when a human is actually needed, and infrastructure that lives in files instead of in somebody's memory.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Most of my work has been on-premises — Proxmox, HA Kubernetes, Gitea, Flux — where there's no managed control plane to hide behind and every failure is yours to explain. The AWS and GCP work came afterwards, and the on-prem years are the reason I trust it.</p>
        <p>Currently in Cairo, working with teams anywhere.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1.1em;">
          <a href="/resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="resume-button">View Resume →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="stack" id="stack">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ comp.page_header({ title: "Stack", level: "h2", cls: "", num: "02" }) }}
    <ol class="stack-index">
      {{ for group of stack }}
      <li class="stack-row">
        <div class="stack-meta">
          <h3 data-count="{{ group.items.length }}">{{ group.name }}</h3>
          <p>{{ group.description }}</p>
        </div>
        {{ comp.tech_tags({ tags: group.items }) }}
      </li>
      {{ /for }}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="windows" id="index">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ comp.page_header({ title: "Index", level: "h2", cls: "", num: "03" }) }}
    <div class="grid">
      <a class="cell" href="/projects">
        <span class="rowline"><span class="truncate">Projects</span><span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="date">→</span></span>
        <p>Infrastructure I've built, broken, and written down afterwards.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="cell" href="/experience">
        <span class="rowline"><span class="truncate">Experience</span><span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="date">→</span></span>
        <p>Where the on-prem lessons came from.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="cell" href="/certifications">
        <span class="rowline"><span class="truncate">Certifications</span><span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="date">→</span></span>
        <p>AWS, Linux Foundation, Huawei.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="cell" href="/blog">
        <span class="rowline"><span class="truncate">Blog</span><span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="date">→</span></span>
        <p>Terminal notes, cleaned up enough to be useful to someone else.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="cell" href="/uses">
        <span class="rowline"><span class="truncate">Uses</span><span class="leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="date">→</span></span>
        <p>Machine, shell, and everything running on it.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
